MC Simulations for Solutes on Water Slabs

slcmd and xSLAB use 500 TIP4P water molecules. They start from
a stored, equilibrated TIP4P water slab containing 512 water molecules.
This file is in the boss/solbox directory.

sl725cmd and xSLAB725 use 725 TIP4P waters. They start from a
regular stored box with 750 waters and discard 25.

There is also a stored, equilibrated water slab with 1235 waters in the
solbox directory.

For a solute z-matrix such as benzen.z, execute via
xSLAB benzen &
or
xSLAB725 benzen &
or
xTEST benzen  (for a short test run)

Equilibration for 5 M and averaging for 25 M.
T = 25 C, P = 1 atm.

Sample output for quadricyclane is in quadric.

The stored  N = 512 and 1235 water slabs are fully equlibrated. You may 
not want to do volume moves when running subsequent slab simulations
as there is a very slow drift to reduce the exposed surface,
i.e. stretch in the z-direction.
